  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Jones County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n Jones County, Iowa\n \nElections\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote\n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections\n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials\n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nPrecinct Officials\n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n Jones County\nElections\n\n\n\n Find your Polling Place and Sample Ballot for the November 3rd Election Click Here \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \nWelcome to the Jones County, Iowa, Elections Website\n The Auditor’s Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find past or upcoming election information.\n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \nWhere's My Absentee Ballot?\n \nWhere Do I Vote?\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n \n\n General Election\n General Election\n \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n \n\n Primary Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n Interactive Results Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n4\n \n \n\n City/School Election\n City/School Election\n \n\n Interactive Results Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \n\n Preparation for the November 3, 2026 General Election\n \n October 15, 2026 \n\n\n\n\n Candidate Paperwork Available\n\n\n\n Election Day: Less than a week away\n\n\nAll News\n \n \n\n \n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nCan I vote for someone that is not on the ballot?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nYes. For each race on the ballot, a line is provided for you to write-in the name of someone for whom you wish to vote for. Make sure you color in the oval! \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nWhat is the last day I can turn in my absentee ballot?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nYou are allowed to hand-deliver your ballot to the Auditor’s office up until the time the polls close on Election Day. If you return your ballot through the mail, your ballot must arrive by 8:00 p.m. on Election Day, with exceptions for individuals in the Safe at Home program and military/overseas citizens. Learn more on our Absentee Voting page. \n\n \n\n \n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n \n \n\n \n Jones County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated October 1, 2026\n \n\n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n5,495\n \n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n5,230\n \n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n2,797\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n74\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 13,596\n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Jones County, Iowa, Elections website at jonescountyiowaelections.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Jones County Auditor\n\n Jones County Courthouse\n \n500 W. Main St., Room 113\n \nP.O. Box 109\n \nAnamosa, IA 52205\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.\n \nMonday - Friday\n \nExtended Hours \n \nPhone Numbers\n\n Office: (319) 462-2282\n \nFax: (319) 462-5815 \n \n\n \n\n Contact Jones County Elections\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
